# `vendor/` AND `public/build/` ARE COMMITTED - see the root `.gitignore` for
# the reasoning and the costs. They are absent from this file rather than
# negated with `!`, because a `!` rule cannot re-include a path whose PARENT
# directory is excluded, and reading two files to work out whether one
# directory ships is how somebody eventually commits a `.env`.
